# Line endings belong to the repository, not to whichever git happens to run.
#
# Two gits share this working tree: Windows git (core.autocrlf=true) and WSL git
# (core.autocrlf=false) reaching it through /mnt/c. Without this file they disagree
# about every text file -- Windows writes CRLF to disk, the repository stores LF,
# and WSL then reports all tracked files as modified when nothing has changed.
#
#   text=auto   normalise to LF inside the repository, whatever the worktree holds
#   eol=lf      and check out LF everywhere, so both gits see identical bytes
#
# Binary files are still detected automatically and left untouched.

* text=auto eol=lf
